{"filePath":"/Users/ai03/Code/Web/truss-3dp-shrinkage-util/truss-webui/src/styles/local.css","newString":"/* --- Inherited properties must be re-established inside the tree ------------ */

/*
 * `:host` is *not* enough for inherited properties, and the reason is a CSS
 * scoping rule rather than a bug: rules in the outer tree take precedence over
 * `:host` rules, so a host page's `* { color: … }` wins on the host element and
 * every shadow descendant inherits it. The app therefore re-establishes its
 * baseline on its own root element, whose rules the page cannot reach — that is
 * what makes "renders identically standalone and embedded" true (decision 13)
 * rather than aspirational.
 *
 * Font *size* is the one thing this cannot fully control: `rem` resolves against
 * the document root even inside a shadow tree, so a host page with a
 * non-default root font-size still scales the widget's rem-based type scale.
 * Setting an explicit `1rem` here stops the host *element*'s font-size from
 * compounding it, which is the part that can be controlled.
 */
.truss-calibrator-root {
  color: var(--text-color-default);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 1rem;
  line-height: 1.5;
  -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  text-size-adjust: 100%;
}

/* --- Layout ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.truss-calibrator-root {
  display: block;
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding: 0.5rem;
  max-width: 700px;
  /* Long words and URLs must wrap rather than widen the widget. */
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
}","oldString":"/* --- Layout ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

.truss-calibrator-root {
  display: block;
  margin-inline: auto;
